# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
# System accounts for CARLOS EMR.
#
# Two accounts, deliberately separate, and neither is a member of any
# privileged group:
#
#   carlos         runs the JVM. Owns the document store and Tomcat's writable
#                  state. Holds the read-write database credential.
#   carlos-backup  runs the backup and restore-drill timers. Holds a
#                  read-only database credential and the restic passphrase,
#                  and owns the backup repository — none of which the `carlos`
#                  uid can read.
#
# The relationship between them is deliberately ONE-WAY. carlos-backup is a
# member of the `carlos` group, so it can READ everything the application owns
# — the document store, carlos.properties, the encryption key the application
# uses for stored credentials — which is exactly what a restorable backup
# needs. `carlos` is NOT a member of any group of carlos-backup's, so the
# application cannot read the repository, the passphrase or the backup
# credential. A compromise of the EMR therefore cannot quietly destroy,
# decrypt or exfiltrate the backups that would be used to recover from it.
#
# The application is NOT run under the distribution's shared `tomcat` user.
# That account is shared with every other Tomcat webapp on the machine, and on
# a host running an EMR that is precisely the boundary that has to hold.
u carlos       - "CARLOS EMR application server" /var/lib/carlos-emr        /usr/sbin/nologin
u carlos-backup - "CARLOS EMR backup" /var/backups/carlos-emr /usr/sbin/nologin
m carlos-backup carlos
